      "body": "This is superseded by #60374, which handles a raising `check_xfer_state` by faulting the peer and keeping the transfer until it drains (or the 10 s drain cap), rather than releasing the handle. Releasing on any raise is unsafe because the WRITE may still be landing (measured in #59790). #49528 is resolved on main. Could you close this one? Thanks for the contribution!\n",
